    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n1 5\n2 1 3 0 1\n1 8\n1 1 3 0 2 0 3 3",
        "output": "5 2 1 0 1\n3 2 1 4 7 8 9 10",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Aarsi took shot on cells (1,2),(1,3),(1,5)(1,2), (1,3), (1,5)(1,2),(1,3),(1,5) while Krypto took shot on cells (1,1),(1,3)(1,1), (1,3)(1,1),(1,3).\nConsidering (1,2)(1,2)(1,2) as the bullseye cell, Aarsi's score would be max⁡(∣1−1∣,∣2−2∣)+max⁡(∣1−1∣,∣2−3∣)+max⁡(∣1−1∣,∣2−5∣)=4\\max(|1-1|,|2-2|) + \\max(|1-1|,|2-3|) + \\max(|1-1|,|2-5|) = 4max(∣1−1∣,∣2−2∣)+max(∣1−1∣,∣2−3∣)+max(∣1−1∣,∣2−5∣)=4. Similarly, Krypto's score would be 222.\nThus, B(1,2)=∣4−2∣=2B_{(1, 2)} = |4-2| = 2B(1,2)​=∣4−2∣=2."
      }
    ]
